  "design": {
    "entrance": "The camera climbs out of a bank of glowing cloud; layered clouds stream past the lens while the pale title descends slowly from above into frame, half-veiled by passing vapour.",
    "reveal": "On the impact frame the sun crests directly behind the letters: volumetric shafts of light fan out around the title and its edges ignite with a warm-white rim.",
    "camera": "Measured vertical ascent (cloud layers parallax downward), slow push; no shake.",
    "material": "Backlit alabaster/ivory stone with soft specular, strong warm-white rim from the sun behind, gentle 2.5D depth; atmospheric scattering softens the far cloud sea.",
    "exit": "The title keeps ascending up and out of frame into the light while the clouds close beneath the camera."
  },
  "fusion_notes": [
    "God rays are made with a Zoom-type DirectionalBlur of the sun disc masked by the inverted title and cloud alpha (no dedicated Rays tool is used, for compatibility). Move SunCore/RaysSmear centre together if you reposition the title."
  ],
